WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.077
"Whoa!" Zann cried as he and Darb ran. "What are those things?"

2
00:00:05.078 --> 00:00:10.148
"I don't know." Darb flapped his hands, trying to ward off the angry little creatures.

3
00:00:10.149 --> 00:00:14.648
They kept diving at the boys, stinging any exposed skin they could reach.

4
00:00:14.649 --> 00:00:19.156
"Let’s go to the Hollow! It's close, and they probably won't follow us there."

5
00:00:19.157 --> 00:00:23.064
Zann glanced in the direction of the Hollow. The place made him nervous.

6
00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:26.894
It was a vacuum and magic didn't work in a vacuum.

7
00:00:26.895 --> 00:00:30.369
Most magical creatures feared and avoided such places.

8
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:34.983
In fact, it was probably the only place Zann would never dare to go.

9
00:00:34.984 --> 00:00:38.355
In the Hollow he'd have no way at all to protect himself.

10
00:00:38.356 --> 00:00:44.780
"I've got a better idea," Zann said. He grabbed Darb's arm and then zapped them both away.

11
00:00:44.781 --> 00:00:48.773
They landed in another part of the swamp, far from the tiny dragons.

12
00:00:48.774 --> 00:00:53.549
"Whew!" Darb grimaced. "Can you do anything about these stings?"

13
00:00:53.550 --> 00:01:01.154
"Hold still." Zann rubbed his hands together and touched the red marks on Darb's arms and face. The marks faded away.

14
00:01:01.155 --> 00:01:03.027
"Thanks," Darb said.

15
00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:08.431
Zann healed his own stings. "So you don't know what those were?" he asked.

16
00:01:08.432 --> 00:01:11.256
"I thought you were an expert in that stuff."

17
00:01:11.257 --> 00:01:17.786
Darb shook his head. "They looked like dragons, but the only dragons that small are mini flowersippers.

18
00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:20.448
And you know what they're like. They don't sting."

19
00:01:20.449 --> 00:01:26.316
"Maybe they're not from Magica!" Zann said. "Maybe there's a wormhole near here."

20
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:29.989
"You mean a portal to another world?" Darb looked doubtful.

21
00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.145
"I thought those were really rare. And really dangerous."

22
00:01:34.146 --> 00:01:38.216
"They are. Most people think my parents got lost in one.

23
00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:42.085
Or maybe went through an unstable one that closed behind them."

24
00:01:42.086 --> 00:01:46.654
Zann started to feel excited. "Let's go back and—oh!"

25
00:01:46.655 --> 00:01:50.905
Zann was nearly knocked off his feet. He grabbed a tree to steady himself.

26
00:01:50.906 --> 00:01:53.093
"What's wrong?" Darb asked.

27
00:01:53.094 --> 00:01:57.105
The feeling had already passed. "It's Boz," Zann said.

28
00:01:57.106 --> 00:02:00.014
"I just felt him. He's not happy."

29
00:02:00.015 --> 00:02:01.925
"Was it a Red Share?"

30
00:02:01.926 --> 00:02:07.531
Zann nodded. A Red Share happened when a Red felt an especially strong emotion.

31
00:02:07.532 --> 00:02:11.214
Any Red with a connection to the other Red would feel it too.

32
00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:15.401
"Boz probably just realized I sneaked out," Zann said.

33
00:02:15.402 --> 00:02:20.422
"It was a strong Share, which means he must be really mad.

34
00:02:20.423 --> 00:02:27.000
Or really scared—he seemed pretty worried about that warning. Either way I'd better get home."

35
00:02:27.001 --> 00:02:32.799
"Okay." Darb tucked an escaping panic bug back into his pocket. "See you tomorrow."

36
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:40.115
"Yeah. If Boz doesn't lock me in the house with a Super Shield spell, that is." Zann rubbed his hands together.

37
00:02:40.116 --> 00:02:48.924
"Focus," he thought. The last thing he needed was to miss his mark and land on the roof or in Zing's food dish. Zap

38
00:02:48.925 --> 00:02:54.168
! He landed in the house's main room. "Right on target!" he

39
00:02:54.169 --> 00:02:57.428
murmured. He glanced around, but Boz was nowhere in sight.

40
00:02:57.429 --> 00:03:04.867
Instead Zann saw a man looking at the family pictures on the wall.

41
00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:09.509
"Who are you?" Zann blurted out. "Where's my grandfather?"

42
00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:15.480
The stranger spun around. He was tall and gaunt, with glittering amber eyes.

43
00:03:15.481 --> 00:03:19.039
An odd expression flickered across his narrow face.

44
00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:28.275
"Another Red," the man said. He pointed at one of the blink images. "Are these your parents, young man?"

45
00:03:28.276 --> 00:03:31.983
Zann noticed his grandfather's diary on the floor under the table.

46
00:03:31.984 --> 00:03:35.767
That was strange. Boz never went anywhere without his diary.

47
00:03:35.768 --> 00:03:38.514
And he'd never leave it lying around on the floor.

48
00:03:38.515 --> 00:03:44.761
"That's none of your business," Zann told the stranger, suddenly nervous. "Where's Boz?"

49
00:03:44.762 --> 00:03:48.169
"Is that any way to speak to a guest in your home?"

50
00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.531
The corners of the man's thin lips twisted into a half smile.

51
00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:56.090
"I happen to be an old friend of your grandfather's."

52
00:03:56.091 --> 00:04:01.651
Zann wasn't sure what to say. "Boz?" he yelled. "Where are you?"

53
00:04:01.652 --> 00:04:06.387
The stranger smirked. "You can call as loudly as you like; he won't hear you.

54
00:04:06.388 --> 00:04:09.823
But I can take you to him if you wish."

55
00:04:09.824 --> 00:04:14.931
"Who are you? What are you doing here?" Zann clenched his fists at his sides.

56
00:04:14.932 --> 00:04:17.601
"And what have you done with Boz?"

57
00:04:17.602 --> 00:04:21.194
Just then he heard scratching at the door. Zing!

58
00:04:21.195 --> 00:04:25.191
Zann quickly rubbed his hands together and pointed at the door. "Open!"

59
00:04:25.192 --> 00:04:31.446
It flew open. Zing leaped into the room, shooting a stream of flame toward the stranger.

60
00:04:31.447 --> 00:04:35.341
"Good boy!" Zann cried. "That'll teach him to—"

61
00:04:35.342 --> 00:04:38.361
But quick as a wink, the stranger lifted his hand.

62
00:04:38.362 --> 00:04:40.662
"No!" shouted Zann.

63
00:04:40.663 --> 00:04:44.179
"Freeze!" said the stranger, pointing at the dragon.

64
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.834
Zing instantly crashed to the floor, not moving.

65
00:04:47.835 --> 00:04:50.679
"Zing!" Zann fell to his knees.

66
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:57.089
Zing was breathing very slowly. Realizing what the man had done, Zann turned to face him.

67
00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:04.081
"You used a Flash Freeze on him!" he accused. "That's illegal! He's a tame dragon!"

68
00:05:04.082 --> 00:05:11.202
Magica had few laws, aside from the important one taught to everyone from birth: Do no harm to others.

69
00:05:11.203 --> 00:05:19.594
But everyone knew that a Flash Freeze should only be used in emergencies such as immobilizing a large, rampaging wild dragon.

70
00:05:19.595 --> 00:05:23.247
It was never supposed to be used on people or pets.

71
00:05:23.248 --> 00:05:32.293
"I never did like dragons," the man said, examining the sparks that still ran across his hand. "Or Reds, for that matter."

72
00:05:32.294 --> 00:05:34.176
He rubbed his fingers together.

73
00:05:34.177 --> 00:05:41.885
Sparks leapt from his hand now, much more strongly than Zann would have expected from such a small amount of friction.

74
00:05:41.886 --> 00:05:45.316
"Freeze!" the man said, pointing toward Zann.

75
00:05:45.317 --> 00:05:50.198
Acting on instinct, Zann quickly grabbed Zing and rubbed his hands together.

76
00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:56.534
He felt the Flash Freeze sizzle within a hairbreadth of his face as he zapped himself and Zing away.

77
00:05:56.535 --> 00:05:59.942
Within half a second, they landed in the front yard.

78
00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:08.550
And half a second after that, Zann's house exploded into a million pieces.

